Initial readiness finishes 231–709 ms before the ordinary Enter input through normal inventory, movement and camera controls. Initial snapshot costs 2.8–3.7 ms; delivery costs 5.8–7.0 ms; worker jobs cost 126.6–252.4 ms. New post-recovery prewarm jobs on diagonal routes are recorded separately and are not first-strike readiness evidence.

This is a development-server measurement on the actual host workload recorded in report.json. First current admission still costs 25.9–33.0 ms and paid frame gaps still reach 66.6–83.3 ms; male routes contain 84/86 ms long tasks. These results establish a bounded improvement, not sustained 60 FPS or complete motion polish. Immediate/unready/stale/failed cues retain original synchronous physical admission and can retain its first-fit hitch.

The preceding report failed only because a recorder assertion counted the intended original recovery delegation as a readiness miss. It remains retained at ../paired-native-original-fallback-no-idle/report.json. The corrected recorder limits that assertion to prepare/contact; the game source was not changed.

